.SS "float schultz_paint_slack (void)"

.PP
How far past a dirty rectangle repainting actually reaches\&. Antialiased coverage extends past a shape's geometry, so every consumer of a dirty rectangle rounds it out to whole pixels with this much slack\&. It is named once so the region that gets repainted and the region that decides what to repaint cannot drift apart\&.
.PP
A function rather than a constant, because a public header carries no macros: a host reading this across a foreign function interface should not have to reproduce a number that only C can see\&.
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The slack, in pixels\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBschultz_rect\fP schultz_rect_intersect (\fBschultz_rect\fP a, \fBschultz_rect\fP b)"

.PP
Computes the overlap of two rectangles\&. Rectangles that merely touch along an edge do not overlap\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIa\fP First rectangle, by value\&. 
.br
\fIb\fP Second rectangle, by value\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The overlapping region, or a zero sized rectangle at the origin when the two do not overlap\&. Test the result with schultz_rect_is_empty rather than comparing against a rectangle\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBschultz_rect\fP schultz_rect_pixel_bounds (\fBschultz_rect\fP rect, float slack)"

.PP
Expands a rectangle outward to whole pixel boundaries\&. Anything that hands a rectangle to an integer pixel API must round outward, never truncate\&. Truncating loses a fraction of a pixel on the far edge, and for a region that moves by a fractional amount each frame that loss accumulates and periodically leaves a column of the previous frame behind\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIrect\fP The rectangle to align, in pixels\&. 
.br
\fIslack\fP Extra margin in pixels, applied on every side before alignment\&. Pass at least 1 for anything antialiased, because coverage bleeds outside the geometric bounds\&. 
.RE
